C-MultiLight dataset.\n\n[2025.09.25] Our paper is accepted by NIPS 2025.\n\n## Overview\n\nOverview of MV-CoLight. (a) We insert a white puppy as the composite object onto the table between basketballs, and render multi-view inharmonious images, background-only images, and depth maps using a camera trajectory moving from distant to close-up positions. (b) We input a single-view data into the 2D object compositing model, which processes the data through multiple Swin Transformer blocks to output the harmonized result. (c) We project the multi-view features from 2D models into Gaussian space via $\\Phi(\\cdot)$, combine them with the original inharmonious Gaussian colors projected into 2D Gaussian color space through $\\Psi(\\cdot)$, and then feed them into the 3D object compositing model. "
